agent-ops task task-9e654f1b-22da-42f5-ac42-27beca2d3ead: Office batch 2: visual overhaul (walled S-flow office)
intent: Replace the Office canvas world with the agreed round-5 design: American open-plan office in six walled rooms (S-flow: planning, implementing, verifying on top; reviewing, integrating, lobby bottom right-to-left), doors between consecutive phases, 24-colour art drawn as char matrices, fixed 576x320 art resolution with integer scaling, all text in an HTML layer, repo-grouped overview grid, avatar only inside a room, actors walking via waypoints on phase change. Remove the hallway, overview avatar, bottom room tabs, dialogue strip and flow strip. Keep the header, repo filter, language toggle, recent toggle, polling, right column (work list / batch-1 room criteria panel) and detail dialogs. Work is split into subtasks S0-S5.
criteria:
- page-integrates: officePage() embeds the new art, layout and renderer; a node:vm client test boots it with a stub canvas, renders the overview and a room, and switches between them without throwing.
- legacy-removed: page.ts no longer contains the hallway, overview supervisor avatar, room-nav tabs, dialogue strip or flow strip (no hallwayBounds, supervisor, room-nav, dialogue, flow identifiers), checked by a test.
  agent-ops task task-7228778b-cbdf-4353-80d6-20de717ef833: S0 art: 24-colour sprites as char matrices
  intent: New runtime/src/office/art.ts ports the approved scratchpad art (lib.mjs, art2.mjs, art5.mjs) to TypeScript: a 24-colour room palette, procedural sprite builders with automatic sel-out outline, all props (cubicle, conference table, chairs, racks, test bench, status board, exec desk, armchair, coffee table, bookcase, shelving, copier, sorting table, hand truck, kitchen counter, fridge, vending machine, water cooler, cafe table, stool, sofa, plants, wall decor), door frames, the criteria whiteboard and head bubbles. Sprites are generated once server side and injected into the page as data.
  criteria:
  - palette-24: art.ts exports a 24-entry room palette keyed 0-9 and a-n, and every generated room sprite uses only those keys or the transparent dot.
  - alert-reserved: Palette key k (alert red) appears only in the allowlisted alert sprites: the ! bubble, failing rack/status board/test bench variants and FAIL notes on the criteria whiteboard.
  - doors-and-board: art.ts provides side-door and front-door sprites in three frames (closed, ajar, open) with stable sizes, and a criteria whiteboard builder that draws one note per criterion status (PASS, FAIL, pending, UNKNOWN) up to 11 notes plus a + slot beyond 12.
  - avatar-roles: Avatar clothing colours come from the role (coordinator, worker, reviewer, visitor, viewer) while hair and skin stay identity-hashed; no avatar colour equals the alert red.
  agent-ops task task-68370ca6-4015-4242-8181-7c983c1de899: S1+S2 layout and render core
  intent: New runtime/src/office/layout.ts is the single geometry source for the 576x320 room: back wall 0-39, row 1 40-151, middle wall 152-191, row 2 192-311, walls at x 188 and 380, six rooms in S-flow, doors between consecutive phases, the lobby entrance, furniture and wall-decor placements, three standing slots per room and the waypoint graph. The client draws each room into an offscreen canvas at 1 art px = 1 px from art.ts sprites and scales it by a whole number only; the canvas draws no text.
  criteria:
  - layout-rules: A test proves for layout.ts: every wall decoration lies inside its wall face, every furniture item lies inside one room and below the top of the wall behind it, and no two furniture footprints overlap.
  - reachable: A breadth-first walk of a 14x4 foot box from the entrance, with walls solid, doors passable and furniture footprints solid, reaches every standing slot of every room; consecutive phases share a door.
  - integer-render: Under the node:vm stub, a room is drawn onto its 576x320 layer with integer fillRect/drawImage coordinates and sizes and zero fillText calls; the on-screen canvas then fills the available area at the room's 9:5 aspect ratio with image smoothing off.
  - board-from-criteria: The planning whiteboard in a room is drawn from that room criteria statuses, so a test room with PASS, FAIL and unverified criteria paints notes in the matching colours.
  agent-ops task task-edc83d7c-e1af-44f1-ade0-8862b1815e80: S3 HTML layer and removals
  intent: All text moves out of the canvas into HTML positioned over it: a HUD strip above the room (room name, criteria progress bar, verify and review badges, open-question count), zone labels per room, and short nameplates over people. Remove the bottom room tabs, the dialogue strip and the flow strip from the markup and the client.
  criteria:
  - hud: In room mode a HUD element above the canvas shows the room title, passed/total criteria, verify and review outcome and the open-question count, rendered with textContent; a client test checks it for a room with a question.
  - labels: Zone labels for the six rooms and one nameplate per person exist as HTML elements whose positions are whole art pixels times the current scale; a test checks one label and one nameplate.
  - removed: The page markup has no #room-nav, #dialogue or #flow element and the client references none of them, checked by a test.
  agent-ops task task-81d40ec8-6d74-446b-96b0-e0c491b9ebb4: S4 repo-grouped overview
  intent: The overview becomes a scrolling HTML grid of equal room cards, one section per repository with a header carrying the repo name and its open-question count. Each card is the room canvas at the shared whole-number scale. Inside a section, rooms with questions come first, then working rooms, then idle ones. Clicking a card or pressing its number key opens the room. The hallway and the overview avatar are gone.
  criteria:
  - grouped: With rooms from two repositories, the overview renders one section per repository in name order, each header showing the repo name and its open-question count; a client test checks it.
  - ordered: Within a section, rooms with open questions come first, then active rooms, then idle or completed ones, keeping snapshot order inside each group; a test checks it.
  - same-scale-open: Every overview card uses the same whole-number scale, and clicking a card or pressing its number key enters that room; a test checks both.
  - collapsible-list: A header button collapses the right-hand work list so the office takes the whole width and expands it again; its aria-expanded and label follow the state, and the choice is remembered in localStorage for the next visit. Covered by a client test.
  agent-ops task task-db93d15e-fb3e-469d-89a7-56afb58e0aae: S5 movement and interaction
  intent: People take a standing slot in the room of their phase and move only when their phase changes, walking room centre to door to room centre along the layout waypoints; a door opens (closed, ajar, open) while someone is within reach and closes after. Inside a room the viewer avatar spawns at the lobby entrance and moves with arrow keys, WASD or a click on the floor, blocked by walls and furniture footprints. Standing near a person shows a speech bubble with their narration; Enter or a click opens their detail. Phase actions animate (typing, whiteboard, verify check, papers, boxes, raised hand) and stop under prefers-reduced-motion.
  criteria:
  - walk-on-phase: When a snapshot moves a person from planning to verifying, the client walks them through the planning-implementing and implementing-verifying doors in order and the doors pass through ajar and open frames while they are near; with no phase change the person does not move. Covered by a client test.
  - avatar-collision: In a room the viewer avatar starts at the entrance, arrow and WASD keys move it, and it cannot enter a wall or a furniture footprint; a client test drives it into both.
  - bubble-and-detail: Standing within reach of a person shows a speech bubble (HTML, textContent) with their narration, and Enter then opens that person detail dialog; a client test checks both.
  - reduced-motion: Under prefers-reduced-motion people and doors jump straight to their final state and phase actions do not animate; a client test checks it.
